{"activity_text": "Anti-Gram+ & Gram-, Antifungal, candidacidal", "article_id": "", "assay_text": "Unknown", "assay_type": "", "comments_text": "Discovery: identified from the venom transcriptome of the spider Argiope bruennichi (Scopoli, 1772) using sequence alignment followed by online prediction tool analysis of a potential amphipathic region. Sequence analysis: APD analysis reveals this sequence is most similar (47.62%) to BjRPS23(67-84) K: 18%; I=F: 12%; GRAVY: 0.46; M Wt: 2010.446; Mol formula: C97H157N23O22; mol ex coeff: 1490. Activity: inhibited Gram+ B. cereus (MIC 4-64 uM) and S-aureus(MIC > 64 uM), Gram- E. coli (MIC 4 uM), MDR P. aeruginosa (MIC 4-64 uM), and fungi C. albicans (MIC 32 uM) and filamentous fungus F. oxysporum (MIC 8 uM). MOA:bacteria: it permeated bacterial membranes. In vitro Toxicity: The peptide showed a low toxicity to HaCaT (TC50 32-64 uM) and hADMSC (human primary mesenchymal stem cells) cells (TC50 64 uM).", "concentration": "", "cytotoxicity_text": "", "hemolytic_activity_text": "", "measure_group": "", "measure_value": "", "pubmed_id": "37577428", "record_granularity": "entry_text", "reference_text": "Front Microbiol. 2023 Jul 28;14:1249175. doi: 10.3389/fmicb.2023.1249175. Pub-Med.", "sequence_key": "APD6:AP03713", "source_id": "AP03713", "source_numeric_id": "03713", "source_path": "APD6/apd6_export/structured/peptides.csv", "source_record_id": "AP03713", "source_table": "peptides.csv", "stability_text": "", "subject_name": "", "target_organism_text": "", "title": "In silico identification of novel antimicrobial peptides from the venom gland transcriptome of the spider Argiope bruennichi (Scopoli, 1772).", "unit": "", "﻿database": "APD6"}
{"activity_text": "Anti-Gram+ & Gram-, Antifungal, candidacidal", "article_id": "", "assay_text": "Unknown", "assay_type": "", "comments_text": "Discovery: identified from the venom transcriptome of the spider Argiope bruennichi (Scopoli, 1772) using sequence alignment followed by online prediction tool analysis of a potential amphipathic region. Sequence analysis: APD analysis reveals this sequence is most similar (42.86%) to Temporin-La K: 18%; I=F: 12%; GRAVY: 0.46; M Wt: 2010.446; Mol formula: C97H157N23O22; mol ex coeff: 1490. Activity: inhibited Gram+ B. cereus (MIC 4-64 uM) and S-aureus(MIC > 64 uM), Gram- E. coli (MIC 8 uM), MDR P. aeruginosa (MIC 4-64 uM), and fungi C. albicans (MIC 32 uM) and filamentous fungus F. oxysporum (MIC 64 uM). MOA:bacteria: it permeated bacterial membranes. In vitro Toxicity: The peptide showed a low toxicity to HaCaT (IC50 ~64 uM) and hADMSC cells (IC50 > 64 uM).", "concentration": "", "cytotoxicity_text": "", "hemolytic_activity_text": "", "measure_group": "", "measure_value": "", "pubmed_id": "37577428", "record_granularity": "entry_text", "reference_text": "Front Microbiol. 2023 Jul 28;14:1249175. doi: 10.3389/fmicb.2023.1249175. Pub-Med.", "sequence_key": "APD6:AP03714", "source_id": "AP03714", "source_numeric_id": "03714", "source_path": "APD6/apd6_export/structured/peptides.csv", "source_record_id": "AP03714", "source_table": "peptides.csv", "stability_text": "", "subject_name": "", "target_organism_text": "", "title": "In silico identification of novel antimicrobial peptides from the venom gland transcriptome of the spider Argiope bruennichi (Scopoli, 1772).", "unit": "", "﻿database": "APD6"}
